    "summary": "Raging Jerry powers an epic Playin' > Uncle John’s > Morning Dew sandwich",
    "blurb": "The second‑set marathon of Playing In The Band → Uncle John's Band → Morning Dew (and the return repeats) is the show’s centerpiece, driven by Jerry’s scorching lead work. Keith adds textured cascades on Wharf Rat while Bob locks in solid rhythm throughout. First‑set material feels uneven, but the overall energy stays high.",
    "review": "Winterland on November 10 1973 finds the Dead firing on all cylinders after a tentative first set that stumbles through early numbers before gaining momentum with Deal and Mexicali Blues. The real fireworks erupt in the second set, where a five‑song sandwich—Playing In The Band → Uncle John's Band → Morning Dew → Uncle John's Band → Playing In The Band—unfolds into a soaring, half‑step‑high jam that showcases Jerry’s raging guitar swirls and relentless soloing. Keith’s cascading keys lift the Wharf Rat segue, and Bob’s rhythm work on Big River feels especially telepathic. While the cassette‑derived soundboard runs a touch sharp and exhibits some wow‑and‑flutter, the mix remains intelligible enough to appreciate the high‑energy improvisations. For listeners seeking the full experience, the “gd73-11-10.sbd.unknown.3290.sbeok.shnf” recording captures this pivotal sandwich despite its pitch quirks and is the recommended source.",
